The dungeon consists of a large central shared chamber with four offshoots that lead to each general's base. This is where the majority of the fighting takes place, with a free-for-all between each god's forces. Apart from [[aviansie]], all other monsters will not retaliate at the aggressor if they are in combat with another monster.

Accessing the bases requires 70 in their respective stat, which cannot be boosted. The Ancient Prison can be accessed by assembling a [[Frozen key (The Frozen Door)|frozen key]], obtained from defeating the four generals. Once used on the [[Frozen Door]], the key disintegrates, but allows for permanent access to the Ancient Prison.

{{clear}}

===Armadyl's Eyrie===
[[File:Armadyl's Eyrie grapple.png|thumb|2020x200px|A player grappling to Armadyl's Eyrie.]]
*Location: South-west
*Requires: {{SCP|Ranged|70|link=yes}} and a [[crossbow (weapon)|crossbow]] with a [[Mith grapple|mithril grapple]]
*Music: [[Armadyl Alliance]]
*General: [[Kree'arra]]

The [[pillar (God Wars Dungeon)|pillar]] at the gap must be grappled using a [[crossbow (weapon)|crossbow]] and a [[Mith grapple|mithril grapple]]. Just inside the Eyrie, there's a [[crate (Armadyl's Eyrie)|crate]] that can be searched for a spare mithril grapple and/or a bronze crossbow if the player does not have a grapple or crossbow in their inventory.

The Eyrie contains Armadylean [[spiritual mage#Armadyl|spiritual mages]], [[spiritual ranger#Armadyl|rangers]], and [[spiritual warrior#Armadyl|warriors]] as well as regular [[aviansie]].

Several minions of [[Zamorak]]: a [[bloodveld#God Wars|bloodveld]], two [[Werewolf#Level 93|werewolves]], and two [[spiritual ranger#Zamorak|Zamorakian spiritual rangers]] who regularly fight with the Armadyleans are also found here.

===Bandos' Stronghold===
[[File:Bandos' Stronghold door.png|thumb|200x200px|The big door, the entrance to Bandos' Stronghold.]]
*Location: North-west
*Requires: {{SCP|Strength|70|link=yes}} and a [[hammer]] ([[warhammers]], the [[Elder maul|Elder Maul]], or the [[Imcando hammer]] will work)
*Music: [[Bandos Battalion]]
*General: [[General Graardor]]

The gong on the [[big door (God Wars Dungeon)|big door]] must be hit with a hammer to enter the chamber. The player will automatically enter the Stronghold when the gong is hit.

To leave, simply walk up next to the door and it will open, or click on the door ('Bang on big door'). The door does not always open. If this happens, walk about 3-4 squares into the Stronghold and try again. (Simply staying next to the door and repeatedly clicking it does not cause it to open.)

Inside the Stronghold Bandos' higher-level forces can be found: Bandosian [[spiritual mage#Bandos|spiritual mages]], [[spiritual ranger#Bandos|rangers]], and [[spiritual warrior#Bandos|warriors]], [[ork]]s, [[Cyclops (God Wars Dungeon)|cyclopes]], and [[jogre#GWD|jogres]].

Several minions of [[Zamorak]]: a [[bloodveld#God Wars|bloodveld]], [[Hellhound#Level 127|hellhound]], [[imp#GWD|imp]], [[Werewolf#Level 93|werewolf]], and two [[Feral Vampyre#Level 77|vampyres]] are found lingering in the Stronghold, most of them regularly fighting the Bandosians.

===Saradomin's Encampment===
[[File:Saradomin's Encampment ropeclimb.png|thumb|200x200px|The first rock in which a rope is required.]]
*Location: South-east
*Requires: {{SCP|Agility|70|link=yes}} (not boostable), 2 [[rope]]s for first-time entry only
*Music: [[Strength of Saradomin]]
*General: [[Commander Zilyana]]

To enter Saradomin's Encampment, a [[rope]] must be tied to [[Rock (God Wars Dungeon)#Upper|a rock]] by the waterfall, and another rope must be attached to [[Rock (God Wars Dungeon)#Lower|another rock]] inside the Encampment to allow full access. Once the ropes are attached they will remain permanently.

Like the main area, all of Saradomin's forces can be found here: [[Knight of Saradomin|Knights]], [[Saradomin priest|priests]], and [[spiritual mage#Saradomin|spiritual mages]], [[spiritual ranger#Saradomin|rangers]], and [[spiritual warrior#Saradomin|warriors]].

Several minions of [[Zamorak]]: two [[Werewolf#Level 93|werewolves]], two [[Feral Vampyre#Level 77|vampyres]], an [[icefiend]], and a [[Gorak#Level 149|gorak]] are in the encampment, fighting the forces of [[Saradomin]].

===Zamorak's Fortress===
[[File:Zamorak's Fortress bridge.png|thumb|200x200px|The broken ice bridge.]]
*Location: North-east
*Requires: {{SCP|Hitpoints|70|link=yes}} (boostable) to cross the river
*Music: [[Zamorak Zoo]]
*General: [[K'ril Tsutsaroth]]

The player's [[prayer point]]s are immediately drained to 0 upon [[Ice bridge|crossing the river]]. In addition to that, the lighting is dimmed and cannot be illuminated by [[light sources]], though it remains fairly easy to see. The light darkens as the player approaches the boss chamber. This darkness can be dispersed by consuming [[Saradomin's light]], a drop from Commander Zilyana.

Inside the fortress many minions of Zamorak can be found: [[spiritual mage#Zamorak|spiritual mages]], [[spiritual ranger#Zamorak|rangers]], and [[spiritual warrior#Zamorak|warriors]], [[imp#GWD|imps]], [[bloodveld#God Wars|bloodveld]], [[Gorak#Level 149|goraks]], and [[Hellhound#Level 127|hellhounds]].

The Fortress is the only one of the four gods' chambers that contains only the minions of its god. No minions of [[Saradomin]], [[Armadyl]], or [[Bandos]] spawn here.

===Ancient Prison===
[[File:Frozen Door.png|thumb|200x200px|The [[Frozen Door]] leading to the Ancient Prison.]]
*Location: South-centre of main chamber, through the [[frozen door]]
*Requires: {{SCP|Agility|70|link=yes}}, {{SCP|Hitpoints|70|link=yes}} (boostable), {{SCP|Ranged|70|link=yes}}, and {{SCP|Strength|70|link=yes}}
*Music: [[The Ancient Prison]], [[Zaros Zeitgeist]] (Nex P1,2), [[The Angel's Fury]] (Nex P3,4,5)
*General: [[Nex]]

The Ancient Prison requires the player to have used a [[Frozen key (The Frozen Door)|frozen key]] on the door to unseal it and access the prison. Followers of the ancient god [[Zaros]] reside within, far stronger than the combatants in the rest of the dungeon. Unlike other chambers, there are no followers of Zamorak in the prison.

The Prison is divided into four rooms; the initial entry room; the main area where Zaros' followers can be fought; a respite area that contains [[Ashuelot Reis]], a nature spirit who can access the player's bank; and Nex's chamber.

The main area of the prison also contains an [[Ancient Forge]], which is used to break down [[Bandos armour]] into [[Bandosian components]] to repair damaged [[Torva armour]] and [[oathplate armour]] into [[oathplate shards]]. If the player logs out in the main area, they will be sent into the entry room upon logging back in. A chest can be found in the entry and respite rooms that players can use to reclaim items if they die while fighting Nex.

The initial entry room contains no monsters and can be entered freely after it has been unsealed as a place of safety.

==Generals==
The generals reside at the end of their strongholds, requiring 40 [[Kill count#Acquiring essence in God Wars Dungeon|essence]] in order to access. This can be lowered by completing tasks from the [[Combat Achievements]] system, and beginning from the hard tier rewards, the chambers can be instanced, requiring 150,000 coins and lowering by 25,000 for each tier above it. The generals and their bodyguards do count towards essence count, which can be used to extend trips within the dungeon indefinitely with the addition of the banking room in Nex's Ancient Prison, as long as they have the kill count required to do so.

In non-instanced chambers, if the general is damaged but no one is inside, they will despawn.

===Armadyl's general===
{{Main|Kree'arra}}
[[File:Fighting Kree'arra.png|thumb|250px|A group of players fighting Kree'arra, the graceful avatar of [[Armadyl]].]]
*Name: [[Kree'arra]]
*Race: [[Aviansie (race)|Aviansie]]
*Level: 580
*Attack style: [[Ranged]], [[Magic]], [[Melee]] (when not under attack)
*Bodyguards: [[Wingman Skree]], [[Flockleader Geerin]], and [[Flight Kilisa]]

Kree'arra is a massive aviansie; like his fellow brethren, he cannot be attacked with any Melee attacks apart from that of a salamander or halberds. He attacks with melee only when he is not under attack. His Ranged and Magic attacks hit all players in his chamber with a whirlwind attack that knocks players back and freezes them. His maximum hit is 69 with Ranged, 26 with Melee and 21 with Magic.
{{Clear}}

===Bandos' general===
{{Main|General Graardor}}
[[File:Fighting General Graardor.png|thumb|250px|A group of players fighting General Graardor, a huge [[Bandos]]ian war chief.]]
*Name: [[General Graardor]]
*Race: [[Ourg]]
*Level: 624
*Attack style: [[Melee]], [[Ranged]]
*Bodyguards: [[Sergeant Strongstack]], [[Sergeant Steelwill]], and [[Sergeant Grimspike]]

General Graardor is a very large, brutal, and heavily armoured ourg. Although he does not wield a weapon, he still hits very hard and should not be underestimated. He uses Melee and Ranged attacks. His Melee attack can hit up to 60, whilst his Ranged attack has a max hit of 35 (and can hit everyone in the room). Therefore, Protect from Melee is recommended for tanks, whilst the rest Protect from Ranged.
{{Clear}}

===Saradomin's general===
{{Main|Commander Zilyana}}
[[File:Fighting Commander Zilyana.png|thumb|250px|A group of players fighting Zilyana, commander of [[Saradomin]]'s forces.]]
*Name: [[Commander Zilyana]]
*Race: [[Icyene]]
*Level: 596
*Attack style: [[Melee]] and [[Magic]]
*Bodyguards: [[Starlight]], [[Growler]], and [[Bree]]

Commander Zilyana is a female [[Icyene]]. Her max hit with Melee is 27 and Magic is 20; lower than the other bosses, albeit being '''very accurate''', and are of the same speed as [[Throwing knife|throwing knives]]. She will only use her magic attack when in melee distance.
{{Clear}}

===Zamorak's general===
{{Main|K'ril Tsutsaroth}}
[[File:Fighting K'ril Tsutsaroth.png|thumb|250px|A group of players fighting K'ril Tsutsaroth, a servant of the god [[Zamorak]].]]
*Name: [[K'ril Tsutsaroth]]
*Race: [[Demon]]
*Level: 650
*Attack style: [[Melee]] and [[Magic]]
*Bodyguards: [[Balfrug Kreeyath]], [[Tstanon Karlak]], and [[Zakl'n Gritch]]

A massive demon that leads Zamorak's forces, K'ril's Magic attacks are relatively weak compared to his Melee attacks. His magical attacks hit a maximum of 30, but are commonly used. His Melee attacks, however, can hit up to 46. He is also capable of using a melee special attack against targets praying [[Protect from Melee]] that hits through prayer and drains half of the target's current prayer points. K'ril can also inflict [[poison]] damage which starts at 16, so it is advisable to bring protection against [[poison]].
{{Clear}}

===Zaros' general===
{{Main|Nex}}
[[File:Fighting Nex.png|thumb|250px|A group of players fighting Nex, one of [[Zaros]]' most powerful generals.]]
*Name: [[Nex]]
*Race: [[Nihil (race)|Nihil]]
*Level: 1001
*Attack style: [[Melee]] and [[Magic]]
*Bodyguards: [[Fumus]], [[Umbra]], [[Cruor]], and [[Glacies]]
A formidable and exceedingly powerful nihil known as the Angel of Death and the fifth general, Nex is an extremely powerful general of Zaros that forced the other four generals to work together to seal her and her armies behind their ancient prison. Unlike the other generals, Nex possesses multiple phases during her fight. She uses the [[Ruinous Powers]], which are not accessible to players.

