==Historical==
The original version of GWD was released on [[28 August]] [[2007]], less than a month after the source code of ''[[Old School RuneScape]]'' (10 August 2007). On the first official release, [[Jagex]] encountered many issues with bugs that arose in the following weeks (28 August 2007) after launch. These issues were fixed before the God Wars Dungeon was implemented into ''Old School RuneScape.''

===Adjustments pre-release===
Fixes included the following:
* Server load - inefficient combat code running on certain monsters caused the servers to struggle.
* [[Safespotting]] in boss rooms - Angled walls and doorways were edited to a rectangular form without angled corners which could be used to safespot bosses in relative safety. [[File:Zilyana's room.png|thumb|212px|[[Commander Zilyana]]'s angled room before being edited.]]
* Monster settings - monsters are now able to walk through one another and players without causing them to be stuck. Certain monsters behavioural flaws were corrected (some monsters used weaponry and combat styles without code to specify how they would do this).
* Excessive adamant bar drops - originally, [[Aviansie]] had a chance of over a 19.5% drop rate of [[Adamantite bar]]s in [[Bank note|bank-note]] form. The developers did not want [[bots]] re-appearing in ''Old School RuneScape'', so to avoid aviansie bots, they only promised to release the GWD if the adamant bars the aviansie dropped were not noted. This has been remedied by having them drop the bars in noted form only when the hard [[Fremennik Diary]] has been completed. In addition, aviansie in the [[Wilderness God Wars Dungeon]] drop noted bars as well, but players can attack aviansie hunters there.
* Minor general bugs:
** [[Slayer]] [[experience]] is awarded if another monster deals the killing blow (assuming the player deals damage).
** A section of the [[Wilderness]] near the GWD entrance had incorrect map blocking causing players to be stuck.
** The familiar check at the GWD entrance was removed due to it not working correctly.
** [[Killcount]] is more reliable (resetting to 0 after re-entering).
** The snow overlay didn't always vanish correctly on leaving the area.
* Changes that passed the feature poll include:
** The four bosses and their bodyguards broadcast messages to all players in their rooms to state what items have been dropped, and to whom.
** The boss room doors are entrances only, and the altars have a '[[Teleport]]' option to let you exit.
** When the four bosses drop stacks of [[herbs]], they now do so in banknote form.
** A [[Staff of the Dead|new magic weapon]] similar in behaviour to the {{RSL|Staff of light}} is dropped by [[K'ril Tsutsaroth]].

===Nex and the Ancient Prison===
On [[20 October]] [[2021]], the [[Frozen Door]] became interactable, with players hearing a threatening voice when interacting with it. This was assumed to be the voice of Nex, which was confirmed shortly thereafter. On the same day, the [[Tombs of Amascut & Nex Rewards Beta]] went live, allowing for beta testing of several proposed rewards from the boss.

After passing a [[Poll:Nex and Old School's Economy Poll|poll]] in November [[2021]], the [[frozen key]] and first chamber in the [[Ancient Prison]] were made accessible on [[16 December]] [[2021]], and the rest of the prison and the Nex boss fight were released on [[5 January]] [[2022]].

There are many differences between Nex in ''RuneScape 3'' and ''Old School RuneScape'':
* Pieces of the frozen key are dropped by each god's followers in their encampments, rather than from the generals and their bodyguards as part of [[The Frozen Door]] miniquest as in ''Old School RuneScape''. It is also a chargeable item, losing charges every time the Ancient Prison is accessed, and permanent access can only be unlocked by paying Ashuelot Reis. In ''Old School RuneScape'', the frozen key is a one-time-use item that permanently grants access to the Ancient Prison the first time it is used.
* The Zarosian followers in the Ancient Prison are living beings, while in ''Old School RuneScape'', the mages, rangers, and warriors are [[spiritual creature]]s.
* The ancient ceremonial set can be used to bypass Zarosian kill count for accessing Nex. In ''Old School RuneScape'', the [[ancient ceremonial set]] has no impact on kill count.
* There is no altar present in Nex's chambers. In ''Old School RuneScape'', one was added that not only allows for [[prayer]] restoration but, if the player is wearing a Zaros-aligned item, also restores [[Hitpoints]], [[Special attacks|special attack energy]], and [[Energy|run energy]].
* 40 Zarosian followers must be killed to gain access to Nex. In ''Old School RuneScape'', 40 [[Kill count#Acquiring essence in God Wars Dungeon|essence]] is still required, but Zarosian followers can provide multiple essence, meaning fewer than 40 kills are required.
* Nex drops the Torva, Virtus, and Pernix armours, as well as the zaryte bow. In ''Old School RuneScape'', her drop table was significantly changed:
** The [[Virtus armour]] was initially planned as the main reward, but player concerns about it devaluing [[ancestral robes]] caused it to be scrapped. It was later added as a drop from [[The Forgotten Four]], a group of four bosses available after completion of [[Desert Treasure II]].
** The [[Torva armour]] became the main reward from Nex, albeit with changes from ''RuneScape 3''. There, Torva is a melee-focused armour that provides a [[Hitpoints]] boost and degrades over time when used. In ''Old School RuneScape'', Torva remains a melee-focused armour, but has no Hitpoints boost and does not degrade. Additionally, it is dropped in a broken state and must be repaired with [[Bandosian components]] (made by breaking down [[Bandos armour]] using the [[Ancient Forge]] added to the Ancient Prison).
** The [[Zaryte bow]] was initially planned as part of Nex's drop table, but was reworked into the [[Zaryte crossbow]]. Nex drops the [[nihil horn]] which can be combined with the [[Armadyl crossbow]] to make the Zaryte crossbow.
*** The [[venator bow]] (later added with the [[Phantom Muspah]]) reuses aspects of the Zaryte's bow design.
** Other drops unique to ''Old School RuneScape'' are the [[ancient hilt]], used to make the [[ancient godsword]], the [[Zaryte vambraces]], [[ancient brew]]s (a Magic-boosting potion), [[nihil shard]]s (used to create the Zaryte crossbow and [[ancient brew]]s), and [[blood essence]] (which improves [[blood rune]] [[Runecraft]]ing)
** The Pernix armour was not added to ''Old School RuneScape''.

==Trivia==
* Along with the [[Ourania Altar]], the God Wars Dungeon is one of a small handful of new updates that recreated content from the original ''RuneScape 2'' using archived assets.
* On release, generals did not despawn if no players were in their chambers. This was added with an [[Update:Easter 2018 Holiday Event|update]] on [[29 March]] [[2018]] to accommodate for [[Ironman]] players.
* An underwater section of the dungeon in [[Zamorak's Fortress]] was originally planned, but scrapped later on in development. Parts of the area could be seen from the entrance to [[Commander Zilyana]]'s room via the use of an [[oculus orb]] before its removal in an [[Update:Christmas 2021|update]].
* Prior to the release of [[Combat Achievements]], access to the God Wars Dungeon was only possible with partial completion of [[Troll Stronghold]]. This means that players with limited builds (such as the [[obby mauler]]) with level 1 Attack can now enter the God Wars Dungeon using [[Ghommal's hilt]], without having to accept the 3000 Attack XP reward from [[Death Plateau]].
